==Reactions==
Banker [[Guillermo Lasso]], the runner-up in the vote, conceded his defeat in broad terms, by stating: “I recognise the triumph of President Correa.”<ref name="Gill"/> Thousands of Correa's backers celebrated in Quito's main square just after the polls closed. Speaking from the balcony of the Presidential Palace, Correa thanked them for their "immense trust.”<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/18/world/americas/rafael-correa-wins-re-election-in-ecuador.html|title=Rafael Correa Wins Re-election in Ecuador|last=Neuman|first=William|date=18 February 2013|work=The New York Times}}</ref>

